 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Level 2 damage rule, plus \"speed\". The battle runs in rounds between the two current front monsters: the one with the higher speed (team A on ties) attacks first, then the other attacks back if it is still alive; the next round uses the current fronts. Each attack appends \"<attacker> attacks <defender> for <damage> damage, <defender> has <h> health left\" where h is the remaining health clamped at 0; a defender whose health drops to 0 or below appends \"<defender> is defeated\" and the next monster of its team comes forward. When a team has no monster left, append \"Team A wins\" or \"Team B wins\" and stop.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
